</div>
<p class=3D"post-modified-info">Last Updated on February 12, 2022</p>
<p><span style=3D"font-size: 14pt;"><strong>Textile Manufacturing Process:<=
br>
</strong></span>Textile is a very widely used term which includes all kinds=
 of fibers (e-g: Cotton , Jute, Wool, Viscose etc), all kinds of process (e=
-g: Spinning, Weaving, <a href=3D"https://fashion2apparel.com/knitting-term=
s-and-definitions/"><strong>Knitting</strong></a>, Dyeing, Printing, Finish=
ing etc), all kinds of machineries (e-g: Spinning Machineries, Weaving Mach=
ineries, Knitting Machineries, Cutting machineries etc), to convert <a href=
=3D"https://fashion2apparel.com/primary-and-secondary-properties-of-textile=
-fibres/"><strong>textile fiber</strong></a> into finished or end use produ=
cts (e-g: Garments, Furnishing Materials, Household Textiles, Medical texti=
les, <a href=3D"https://fashion2apparel.com/technologies-involved-in-smart-=
textiles/"><strong>Smart Textiles</strong></a>, Shoes Textiles, Fishing Net=
s etc). Textile manufacturing is a very complex and lengthy process. It is =
based in the conversion of three types of fiber into yarn, then fabric, the=
n textiles. These are then fabricated into clothes or other artifacts.</p>
<p>A textile product passes through several processes in its manufacturing =
before it becomes wearable. These processes include spinning, weaving, knit=
ting, wet processing and garments manufacturing. The flow chart of textile =
manufacturing process is shown in Figure 1.</p>
<figure id=3D"attachment_4789" aria-describedby=3D"caption-attachment-4789"=
 style=3D"width: 463px" class=3D"wp-caption aligncenter"><img fetchpriority=
=3D"high" decoding=3D"async" class=3D"size-full wp-image-4789" src=3D"https=
://fashion2apparel.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/02/Textile-manufacturing-pro=
cess.jpg.webp" alt=3D"Textile manufacturing process" width=3D"473" height=
=3D"431"><figcaption id=3D"caption-attachment-4789" class=3D"wp-caption-tex=
t">Figure 1: Textile manufacturing process</figcaption></figure>
<div class=3D"f0a563704b9a4ad93ce1721e45667a12" data-index=3D"3" style=3D"f=
loat: none; margin:10px 0 10px 0; text-align:center;">

<!-- Fashion -->
<ins class=3D"adsbygoogle" style=3D"display:block" data-ad-client=3D"ca-pub=
-7527879365655387" data-ad-slot=3D"7501605594" data-ad-format=3D"auto" data=
-full-width-responsive=3D"true" data-adsbygoogle-status=3D"done" data-ad-st=
atus=3D"filled"><iframe id=3D"aswift_2" name=3D"aswift_2" data-load-complet=
e=3D"true"></iframe></ins>

</div>


<p><strong>Normally, the whole textile manufacturing process is divided by =
four branches. These are:</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Yarn Manufacturing or Spinning.</li>
<li>Fabric Manufacturing or Weaving.</li>
<li>Dyeing, Printing and Finishing</li>
